  [PASS] h_W table (150 -> 300) and the log2 counts at m = 300 reproduced to 4 decimals
  [PASS] thresholds (1-h*)/(1-h_W): 0.20 (W=4), 0.47 (W=8), 0.77 (W=16)
  [CLAIM OK] section 3: h_W table (exact DP, tie rule S_j = -j in [-W,0] iff j <= W), W = 1 empty for m >= 3, thresholds 0.20/0.47/0.77 L  -- the 4-decimal values are 150->300 growth rates; the 300->600 rates differ by up to 0.0029, so "PROVED numerically" means +-0.003
  the "one-sided 0.94996" entry is the limit h*, not a 150->300 growth rate (which would be h* - 1.5*log2(2)/150 = 0.9400): cosmetic.
  consequence check: #words with a [-W,0]-hover of length m <= L is 2^(h_W m + o(m)); each is one class mod 2^m with <= X/2^m + 1 elements in [1, X];
  so the count is <= X 2^(-(1-h_W) m + o(m)) for m <= L, and it is <= X^(h* + o(1)) once m >= (1-h*)/(1-h_W) L. Elementary; the exponent o(1) is omitted in the note.

[4] Section 8 (leaders and peaks)
  [PASS] carry beta_s has the sign of b and |beta_s| <= |b|((3/2)^s - 1) (exhaustive, s <= 12, b in {1,-1,3,-5})
  (i) leaders: y_(i+s) = M_s y_i + beta_s > y_i with |beta_s| <= |b|(3/2)^k <= Y_0/2 <= y_i/2 gives M_s > 1 - |beta_s|/y_i >= 1/2: direction right.
  [CLAIM OK] section 8 (i): leaders, M_s > 1 - |beta_s|/y_i >= 1/2, all partial sums > -1, counted by M_k(1)
  (ii) peaks. Version at commit 3987cf42b (the text this audit was commissioned on): "M_k > M_s (1 - o(1)), i.e. the word ends within
       0.01 bits of its strict maximum": NOT what y_i >= Y_0 gives (see the witness below); the count then used M_k(1.6), inconsistent with 0.01.
       Version at commit ab9ef18b4 (revised during this audit, now in the worktree): "M_k > M_s - (|beta_k| + |beta_s|)/z >= M_s - 1" and
       "(s = 0) M_k z + beta_k > z, so M_k > 1/2", then the two cases M_s >= 3/2 / M_s < 3/2 give M_k/M_s > 1/3. The step ">= M_s - 1"
       needs z = y_(i-k) >= |beta_k| + |beta_s|, and "M_k > 1/2" by that route needs z >= 2|beta_k|; the hypothesis is y_i >= Y_0, which
       bounds nothing about z (z < y_i is all that is known). Neither inequality is derived: a gap in the proof as written.
       Correct argument needing only y_i >= Y_0: M_k z = y_i - beta_k >= y_i - Y_0/2 >= y_i/2 and M_s z = y_(i-k+s) - beta_s < y_i + Y_0/2 <= (3/2) y_i,
       so M_k/M_s > 1/3 = 0.3333 > 2^(-1.6) = 0.3299, i.e. S_k - S_s > -log_2 3 = -1.585 > -1.6 for every 0 <= s < k (s = 0 gives M_k > 1/2).
       With the carry sign: b > 0 gives M_s z <= y_(i-k+s) < y_i and M_k/M_s > 1/2 (S_k - S_s > -1); b < 0 gives the ratio > 2/3.
       z cancels; no condition on z or on the intermediate values is needed. The count by M_k(1.6) stands (1.6 is the right constant: 1/3 > 2^-1.6).
       (Alternative repair of the z-route: peaks with y_(i-k) < Y_0 number at most Y_0 since i -> y_(i-k) is injective; assume z >= Y_0 for the rest.)
       search: 16008 peaks at index k (k = 8..16, z < 2^15, y_k >= Y_0): peaks with z < |beta_k| + |beta_s| for some s: 0; violations of M_k > M_s - 1: 0
       (so the revised chain is not refuted by examples; it is unproved as written. Note for b = 1 it can be proved differently: a violation
       M_k <= M_s - 1 with y_k >= Y_0 forces z > (3/2)^(k-s) while the peak condition forces the suffix carry gamma > z, but gamma <= (3/2)^(k-s) - 1.)
  [CLAIM FALSE] section 8 (ii): the displayed justification of M_k/M_s > 1/3 is complete as written (either version)  -- 3987cf42b: "(1 - o(1))/0.01 bits" false at the threshold; ab9ef18b4: divides by z without a lower bound on z
  [CLAIM OK] section 8: Proposition statement (leaders and peaks <= X are O(X^(h*) L^(-3/2)) + 2|b| X^0.585 + k)  -- with the y_i-comparison closing the peak case
       witness: all-odd word, b = 1, y_i = Y_0 = 2(3/2)^k: (y_i - beta_k)/y_i = 0.5002 (= 1/2 + o(1)), so M_k z is only y_i/2: "1 - o(1)" fails at the stated threshold.
  (iv) leaders/peaks on long segments, k = L, X = 2^L (window form: y_(i+s) > y_i resp. y_(i-s) < y_i for 1 <= s <= k, which
